Assuming an invalid coordinate should return `0`, values are nonnegative, and the values are small enough to fit in an `int`:

```java
public int coordinateFactorialValue(int[][] grid, int row, int col) {
    if (grid == null ||
        row < 0 || row >= grid.length) {
        return 0;
    }

    int[] currentRow = grid[row];

    if (currentRow == null ||
        col < 0 || col >= currentRow.length) {
        return 0;
    }

    int num = currentRow[col];

    if (num < 0) {
        return 0; // or throw an exception, depending on the specification
    }

    int factorial = 1;

    for (int i = 2; i <= num; i++) {
        factorial *= i;
    }

    return factorial;
}
```

